      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;max-width:700px;">
        BoldLeads is a lead-generation subscription for real estate agents — it runs Facebook ads, captures seller leads, and charges you a monthly fee plus a required ad budget. BirkyStudio takes a different route: we hand you a verified, enriched, scored list of real prospects you own forever, and our AI follows them up the moment they respond. One is a never-ending subscription you rent. The other is a deliverable you keep. Here's the honest breakdown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section style="padding:80px 0;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a0f2e 0%,#2d1b4e 100%);">
    <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 32px;">

      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1e1b4b,#312e81);border-radius:16px;padding:32px;margin-bottom:64px;border:1px solid rgba(129,140,248,0.3);">
        <h2 style="color:white;font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:16px;">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BirkyStudio if:</strong> You want real, verified prospects delivered once and owned forever — with an AI that catches and qualifies replies the moment they come in. Best for agents tired of paying a subscription for leads they don't trust and don't own.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">Choose BoldLeads if:</strong> You want a self-serve, continuous flow of fresh exclusive-by-ZIP leads generated by Facebook ads, and you're willing to pay $399-$799/month plus $500-$1,000/month in ad spend to run and manage those campaigns yourself. Best for agents who want volume and don't mind the subscription.<br><br>
          <strong style="color:white;">The honest difference:</strong> BoldLeads charges you every month and keeps you locked in. BirkyStudio charges once and hands you the prospects — plus an AI that does the follow-up BoldLeads leaves to you.
        </p>
