        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          BoldLeads is an established real estate lead-generation platform. It runs exclusive Facebook ads targeted to specific ZIP codes, captures homeowners who request a home valuation, and delivers those seller leads to you. It includes a CRM, landing pages, and autoresponders, and can be set up with a concierge. Its pricing runs $399-$799/month for the platform, plus $500-$1,000/month in required ad spend.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          When it works, the model is proven: agents get a continuous flow of leads exclusive to their ZIP, and the system handles the ad management. It's a self-serve machine you operate. But that's the catch — it only works if the leads are worth calling and if you keep paying. Agents who cancel report losing access to the leads, the CRM, and the landing pages.
        </p>
        <p style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:16px;">
          The reviews tell a rough story. BoldLeads carries a low average rating, and the recurring complaints are consistent: lead quality collapsing, leads that are bots or scams, and difficulty cancelling. Reddit agents describe lead quality that "has fallen off the table and simultaneously gotten 2-3x more expensive," and call the leads "bots, scams, kids." There are dozens of 1-star reviews about billing after cancellation.
        </p>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px;margin-bottom:16px;">
          <div>
            <p style="color:white;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:8px;">✅ Pros</p>
            <ul style="color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;">
